(text "The combined sense resistance is 90mOhm. Kelvin-route IN and SENSE to the resistor pair; no load copper in the pickups." (at 849.63 1029.97 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid d9884b4b-18f6-5163-b405-7e4e86a95473))
(text "U718 supplies the fast UV/OV protection. U2660 UV/OV inputs are disabled; its current limiter and timer remain active." (at 849.63 1040.13 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 188538f0-76aa-517f-bcc7-ec934ab6b9fc))
(text "After fixing a standby short, remove all power or momentarily short TP2660 to TP2661 to reset the latch. This also restarts the EC." (at 849.63 1050.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 7b596243-9dc5-553f-a9ae-fe0808987ebf))
(text "J190 is the single AUX/SOLAR physical input; USB-C PD negotiation remains only on sheet 5." (at 379.73 20.32 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 70bc4b9a-454b-5f64-8e40-b43eca7a8191))
(text "TPS26630 accepts 7-22V nominal; 0.1% ladder targets 5.53V/22.99V rising UV/OV and a 3A limit." (at 379.73 25.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 837be228-a7b0-5129-8fe4-82fa66189ead))
(text "U15/U16 accepts fixed 5/9/15/20V PD contracts and AUX across 7-22V; priority remains PD1 > PD2 > AUX." (at 379.73 31.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid ea55f9e2-0756-5d58-8e45-57454b153710))
(text "SMCJ24CA protects the AUX eFuse input. The common LTC4418 window protects the charger input." (at 379.73 38.1 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 128bb12f-9be5-597b-b34f-48b8c78b9849))
(text "NOTE: no wires used - connectivity is via matching label names (valid KiCad practice)." (at 20.32 219.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid e6956020-68ea-531d-9d6b-716f1e55f149))
(text "BMS J2 carries raw pack power; J2201 carries the two midpoint taps. Verify connector polarity before connecting cells." (at 20.32 226.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 3080f9f8-e71d-576b-9adb-157049221bfd))
(text "U719 BQ76922 protects the three cells and drives high-side charge/discharge FETs from its verified configuration." (at 20.32 232.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid d37449ac-51bd-5140-8d72-749ffd175f8b))
(text "RS11 is a four-terminal2mOhm shunt. Independent current guards, native cell/current protection and F1 cover the battery path." (at 20.32 237.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 5c54854a-3d39-5129-a765-434a35879953))
(text "Three insulated cell probes drive independent raw-referenced charge/discharge inhibits on the BMS." (at 20.32 243.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 0865e845-1da1-5209-a573-6dc4430b36a1))
(text "Charging requires verified BMS status and bounded EC source/current settings. The raw BMS charge inhibit remains independent." (at 20.32 250.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 277ea3d8-e018-56d8-975e-f79a915fb30e))
(text "ISL9241 starts with a 200mA input limit and charging off. Firmware must verify the source and program bounded limits." (at 20.32 256.54 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 6c0d9f52-0965-5a6c-898b-8676d2a9a159))
(text "J190 is the one 7-22V nominal AUX input; TPS26630 protects it before the source selector." (at 20.32 264.16 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid c3404481-d196-51be-9eee-af9a9ed41743))
(text "AUX current is limited by the released source profile. Solar MPPT is not implemented in this charger driver." (at 20.32 271.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 30d7ff3b-4525-59bb-9e6c-e0e864a06d96))
(text "AUX_DC_ADC measures the protected input so firmware can detect droop and reduce charger input current." (at 20.32 287.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 520d73f3-4ca6-55e3-a929-dcf8199f0fc3))
(text "RS2600 is the 20mOhm input shunt. RS2601 is the separate 10mOhm battery-current shunt; both need Kelvin routing." (at 20.32 294.64 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 45df285f-f605-544c-8d95-e092251a5faf))
(text "Q25 is the ISL9241 battery-path FET. Battery standby comes through VSYS and the discharge shunt; disabling Mu keeps button wake available." (at 20.32 302.26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 08919e9e-575f-5edc-83c5-6dc79782f6fe))
(text "U11 accepts about 8.45-13.57V nominal; 11mOhm RS10 gives 4.55A nominal and <=5.51A worst-case trips." (at 20.32 309.88 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 3b329d5d-0b9b-5b2e-951d-5629b5f645c7))
(text "The charger NTC pin receives a hardware inhibit from the BMS permit. The fixed 10k state is not a cell-temperature measurement." (at 20.32 317.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 16e31804-38c4-53bf-8ae0-d958cdf93d76))
(text "STARTUP: keep Mu enable low and PROCHOT asserted. Read TCPC PD Status 0x40 and active PDO/RDO 0x34/0x35 before selecting a source." (at 20.32 325.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 33708f5f-c187-5ea9-91b1-f0152cc89a88))
(text "Require the qualified VSYS threshold before Mu enable and confirm MU_12V_PG. Source, charger, watchdog or PG faults revoke enable; profile gates remain off until qualified." (at 20.32 332.74 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 71377c09-3cab-57fa-aefa-7c294dd5f2ce))
(text "The charger watchdog stays enabled. JEITA, source limits and throttle settings must be read back before the hardware gates are released." (at 20.32 340.36 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 61ef3747-815e-57e6-b5f1-d05628da3fdc))
(text "U718 provides fast voltage protection. U2660 limits standby inrush and latches a persistent fault; TP2660/TP2661 provide a service reset." (at 20.32 347.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 49e520dd-4345-5904-982f-6d24f0ca6baa))
(text "USB and VSYS use reverse-blocking ideal-diode feeds. AUX uses D711. The EC can start from 5V USB before the main source paths are enabled." (at 20.32 355.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid bbe89f66-9247-5441-8207-faed32b97f46))
(text "5V and 9V adapters use the buck-boost path. Running and charging share the measured input budget; a qualified pack can cover a shortfall." (at 20.32 363.22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid 415f9602-218b-5cb5-8690-bebb6699c474))
(text "C746 provides low-ESR hold-up through LTC4418 break-before-make source switching." (at 20.32 370.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left)) (uuid fd37e03e-a691-55f0-a403-32028008c54d))
